# Check loaded data at the boundary

## Description

Data from files, databases and APIs is untrusted in the same way request payloads are. An array or a frame with a renamed column, a changed dtype or a wrong shape usually does not crash; it produces plausible-looking wrong results. Right after a load, a small check compares what arrived with what the code expects and raises an error that names the column or array, its actual dtype or shape, and the expected one. Everything downstream then relies on that check.

